cf-feat-absorb-strength = Absorb Strength
cf-feat-absorb-strength-desc = One action, once an hour, beside an enemy that died in the last minute: temporary Hit Points equal to its level for a minute. TBA
cf-feat-adapted-cantrip = Adapted Cantrip
cf-feat-adapted-cantrip-desc = Requires a spellcasting class. A cantrip from any tradition, chosen here, cast as your class casts.
cf-feat-adaptive-adept = Adaptive Adept
cf-feat-adaptive-adept-desc = Requires Adapted Cantrip and rank 3 spells. A cantrip or rank 1 spell from that tradition, cast as your class casts. TBA
cf-feat-adaptive-vision = Adaptive Vision
cf-feat-adaptive-vision-desc = +1 circumstance to saves against visual effects, and a success becomes a critical success.
cf-feat-affliction-resistance = Affliction Resistance
cf-feat-affliction-resistance-desc = +1 circumstance to saves against diseases and poisons, and a success becomes a critical success.
cf-feat-ageless-patience = Ageless Patience
cf-feat-ageless-patience-desc = Take twice as long on a Perception or skill check for a +2 circumstance bonus, and a natural 1 is not worse. TBA
cf-feat-agonizing-rebuke = Agonizing Rebuke
cf-feat-agonizing-rebuke-desc = After you Demoralize an enemy it takes 1d4 mental damage each turn while frightened and within 30 feet, up to a minute. TBA
cf-feat-alchemical-scholar = Alchemical Scholar
cf-feat-alchemical-scholar-desc = You gain the Alchemical Crafting feat (TBA).
cf-feat-allys-shelter = Ally's Shelter
cf-feat-allys-shelter-desc = A reaction, automatic, once a day: a save that would fail uses the modifier of an ally within 5 feet, when that is better than yours and would change the result.
cf-feat-ancestral-longevity = Ancestral Longevity
cf-feat-ancestral-longevity-desc = You are trained in one skill of your choice, chosen here. Swapping it each day: TBA
cf-feat-ancestral-suspicion = Ancestral Suspicion
cf-feat-ancestral-suspicion-desc = +2 circumstance bonus to saves against being controlled, and a success on one is a critical success. TBA
cf-feat-anchoring-roots = Anchoring Roots
cf-feat-anchoring-roots-desc = You gain the Steady Balance feat (TBA). Anchor, the action that roots you against being moved: TBA
cf-feat-animal-accomplice = Animal Accomplice
cf-feat-animal-accomplice-desc = You gain the Pet feat (TBA): a familiar, which the game does not have yet.
cf-feat-animal-elocutionist = Animal Elocutionist
cf-feat-animal-elocutionist-desc = Speak with animals and use Diplomacy on them, with +1 circumstance to Make an Impression. TBA
cf-feat-aquatic-elf-warrior = Aquatic Elf Warrior
cf-feat-aquatic-elf-warrior-desc = For proficiency, you treat crossbows, heavy crossbows, daggers, longspears, spears and tridents one category simpler. Fighting underwater: TBA
cf-feat-askthe-bones = Ask the Bones
cf-feat-askthe-bones-desc = A free action once a day: Recall Knowledge through a dead friend's bone, with +1 circumstance if they knew the subject. TBA
cf-feat-athletic-might = Athletic Might
cf-feat-athletic-might-desc = A success on a check to Climb is a critical success. The same for Swim: TBA
cf-feat-beast-trainer = Beast Trainer
cf-feat-beast-trainer-desc = Trained in Nature. Grants an item. Not added in play yet.
cf-feat-benefactors-resistance = Benefactor's Resistance
cf-feat-benefactors-resistance-desc = Requires the dragonscaled kobold heritage. Choose your benefactor's breath here. You resist that damage equal to half your level.
cf-feat-benefactors-strike = Benefactor's Strike
cf-feat-benefactors-strike-desc = Requires the dragonscaled kobold heritage. A critical hit with an unarmed Strike deals 1 persistent damage of your benefactor's breath. TBA
cf-feat-blast-resistance = Blast Resistance
cf-feat-blast-resistance-desc = Resistance 3 to fire and sonic. The better saves against dazzled and deafened: TBA
cf-feat-bloody-blows = Bloody Blows
cf-feat-bloody-blows-desc = A critical hit with a lethal unarmed Strike deals 1d4 persistent bleed. TBA
cf-feat-bone-magic = Bone Magic
cf-feat-bone-magic-desc = Choose one occult or primal cantrip. You can cast it at will.
cf-feat-boulder-roll = Boulder Roll
cf-feat-boulder-roll-desc = Requires Rock Runner. Two actions: Step into an enemy your size or smaller, pushing it back unless it holds with a Fortitude save against your Athletics DC. TBA
cf-feat-bounce-boost = Bounce Boost
cf-feat-bounce-boost-desc = Requires trained in Athletics. A reaction: an adjacent ally who jumps gets +1 circumstance and a few feet more. TBA
cf-feat-briny-beverage = Briny Beverage
cf-feat-briny-beverage-desc = Requires the kijimuna heritage, which the game does not have. Drink salt water, and once a day feel the water around you. TBA
cf-feat-burn-it = Burn It!
cf-feat-burn-it-desc = A status bonus to the fire damage of your spells and alchemical items, at least +1, and +1 status to persistent fire damage. TBA
cf-feat-cantorian-reinforcement = Cantorian Reinforcement
cf-feat-cantorian-reinforcement-desc = A success on a save against a disease or poison becomes a critical success.
cf-feat-cat-nap = Cat Nap
cf-feat-cat-nap-desc = Once an hour, 10 minutes of sleep gives you temporary Hit Points equal to your level for an hour. TBA
cf-feat-catfolk-dance = Catfolk Dance
cf-feat-catfolk-dance-desc = Catfolk Dance, one action: Acrobatics against an adjacent creature's Reflex DC. On a success it takes -2 circumstance to Reflex saves for 6 seconds, and a critical success also leaves it off-guard.
cf-feat-catfolk-lore = Catfolk Lore
cf-feat-catfolk-lore-desc = Lore: Catfolk Lore. Trained in Acrobatics and Survival.
cf-feat-catfolk-weapon-familiarity = Catfolk Weapon Familiarity
cf-feat-catfolk-weapon-familiarity-desc = For proficiency, you treat catfolk weapons, the kama, kukri, scimitar and sickle one category simpler: martial as simple, advanced as martial. At level 5, a critical hit with one of them gets its critical specialization. Access to uncommon weapons: TBA
cf-feat-cats-luck = Cat's Luck
cf-feat-cats-luck-desc = Free and automatic, once per long rest. Reroll a failed Reflex save and use the better result.
cf-feat-charmed-sleep = Charmed Sleep
cf-feat-charmed-sleep-desc = While asleep you look like a small object, with +4 status to Deception to pass for one. TBA
cf-feat-cheek-pouches = Cheek Pouches
cf-feat-cheek-pouches-desc = Store up to four light items in your cheeks with an Interact action. TBA
cf-feat-childlike-plant = Childlike Plant
cf-feat-childlike-plant-desc = Requires chrysanthemum leshy heritage or peachchild leshy heritage. Trained in Deception. +4 circumstance bonus to Deception. Not applied in play yet.
cf-feat-city-scavenger = City Scavenger
cf-feat-city-scavenger-desc = +1 circumstance to Subsist, and you can Subsist in a settlement with Society or Survival while Earning Income. TBA
cf-feat-clan-pistol = Clan Pistol
cf-feat-clan-pistol-desc = Trained in the clan pistol, and one for free. +1 circumstance to Make an Impression on Dongun Hold folk when it shows. Firearms: TBA
cf-feat-clever-improviser = Clever Improviser
cf-feat-clever-improviser-desc = You gain the Untrained Improvisation feat (TBA).
cf-feat-clever-shadow = Clever Shadow
cf-feat-clever-shadow-desc = Your shadow can do simple things within your reach, such as open an unlocked door. TBA
cf-feat-climbing-claws = Climbing Claws
cf-feat-climbing-claws-desc = A climb Speed of 10 feet: climbing needs no check.
cf-feat-cooperative-nature = Cooperative Nature
cf-feat-cooperative-nature-desc = +4 circumstance bonus to Aid. TBA
cf-feat-cornered-fury = Cornered Fury
cf-feat-cornered-fury-desc = When a bigger creature critically hits you, it is off-guard to you for a round. TBA
cf-feat-cringe = Cringe
cf-feat-cringe-desc = A reaction, automatic: when a Strike critically hits you, its damage drops by your level + 2. The attacker being immune for a day: TBA
cf-feat-croak-talker = Croak Talker
cf-feat-croak-talker-desc = Speak with amphibians and use Diplomacy on them. TBA
cf-feat-crocodiles-twin = Crocodile's Twin
cf-feat-crocodiles-twin-desc = Requires the bakuwa or makari heritage, which the game does not have. A Tiny crocodile familiar. TBA
cf-feat-crunch = Crunch
cf-feat-crunch-desc = Your jaws deal 1d8 piercing damage instead of 1d6. The grapple trait: TBA
cf-feat-cultural-adaptability = Cultural Adaptability
cf-feat-cultural-adaptability-desc = You gain the Adopted Ancestry feat (TBA). A level 1 ancestry feat from that ancestry: TBA
cf-feat-defy-death = Defy Death
cf-feat-defy-death-desc = Requires Orc Ferocity. Your recovery checks are 1 easier, and coming back from the dead by magic leaves you no worse for it.
cf-feat-defythe-darkness = Defy the Darkness
cf-feat-defythe-darkness-desc = Requires darkvision. Greater darkvision sees through magical darkness, and you cannot use darkness effects. TBA
cf-feat-distant-cackle = Distant Cackle
cf-feat-distant-cackle-desc = Requires the witch kholo heritage. Cast ventriloquism once a day as an occult innate spell. TBA
cf-feat-distracting-shadows = Distracting Shadows
cf-feat-distracting-shadows-desc = Creatures a size larger than you count as cover to Hide and Sneak behind. TBA
cf-feat-dokkaebi-fire = Dokkaebi Fire
cf-feat-dokkaebi-fire-desc = Requires the dokkaebi heritage, which the game does not have. An ignition cantrip that deals illusory mental damage. TBA
cf-feat-dongun-education = Dongun Education
cf-feat-dongun-education-desc = Two of Engineering, Explosive and Firearm Lore, rising to expert at level 2. TBA
cf-feat-draconic-sycophant = Draconic Sycophant
cf-feat-draconic-sycophant-desc = +2 circumstance to Perception and saves against dragons. The quick Make an Impression: TBA
cf-feat-dragons-presence = Dragon's Presence
cf-feat-dragons-presence-desc = Requires the dragonscaled kobold heritage. A success on a save against fear is a critical success. A failure becoming a critical failure, and +1 to Demoralize weaker foes: TBA
cf-feat-dragonscaled-lore = Dragonscaled Lore
cf-feat-dragonscaled-lore-desc = Requires dragonscaled kobold heritage. Lore: Dragon Lore. Trained in Intimidation. Trained in a skill of your choice. That choice is not recorded yet.
cf-feat-duck = Duck!
cf-feat-duck-desc = A Reflex save against an area effect from a Huge or bigger creature is one degree better. TBA
cf-feat-dwarven-doughtiness = Dwarven Doughtiness
cf-feat-dwarven-doughtiness-desc = Frightened eases by 2 each turn instead of 1.
cf-feat-dwarven-lore = Dwarven Lore
cf-feat-dwarven-lore-desc = Lore: Dwarf Lore. Trained in Crafting and Religion.
cf-feat-dwarven-reinforcement = Dwarven Reinforcement
cf-feat-dwarven-reinforcement-desc = Requires expert in Crafting. An hour's work gives part of a building +1 Hardness for a day. TBA
cf-feat-dwarven-weapon-familiarity = Dwarven Weapon Familiarity
cf-feat-dwarven-weapon-familiarity-desc = For proficiency, you treat dwarf weapons, the battle axe, pick and warhammer one category simpler: martial as simple, advanced as martial. At level 5, a critical hit with one of them gets its critical specialization. Access to uncommon weapons: TBA
cf-feat-eat-fortune = Eat Fortune
cf-feat-eat-fortune-desc = A reaction once a day: when a creature within 60 feet uses a fortune or misfortune effect, you undo it. TBA
cf-feat-elemental-spark = Elemental Spark
cf-feat-elemental-spark-desc = Requires Sprite's Spark. The spark reaches 30 feet and deals the damage of an element you choose. The spark itself is not built. TBA
cf-feat-elven-lore = Elven Lore
cf-feat-elven-lore-desc = Lore: Elf Lore. Trained in Arcana and Nature.
cf-feat-elven-persistence = Elven Persistence
cf-feat-elven-persistence-desc = Free and automatic, once per long rest. A failed check with a skill you are trained in becomes 12 plus your proficiency bonus instead.
cf-feat-elven-weapon-familiarity = Elven Weapon Familiarity
cf-feat-elven-weapon-familiarity-desc = For proficiency, you treat elf weapons, longbows, composite longbows, rapiers, shortbows and composite shortbows one category simpler: martial as simple, advanced as martial. At level 5, a critical hit with one of them gets its critical specialization. Access to uncommon weapons: TBA
cf-feat-energized-font = Energized Font
cf-feat-energized-font-desc = Requires a focus pool and a gnome innate spell of a focus spell's tradition. One action, once a day: regain 1 Focus Point. TBA
cf-feat-envenom-fangs = Envenom Fangs
cf-feat-envenom-fangs-desc = Requires Iruxi Armaments (fangs). Envenom Fangs, one action, once a day: your next unarmed Strike within 6 seconds that hits adds 1d6 persistent poison. The rules allow it once an hour.
cf-feat-expert-drill-sergeant = Expert Drill Sergeant
cf-feat-expert-drill-sergeant-desc = Allies who Follow the Expert behind you gain +3, or +4 at master. TBA
cf-feat-explosive-savant = Explosive Savant
cf-feat-explosive-savant-desc = Bombs and martial firearms count as simple weapons for your proficiency, and advanced firearms as martial. TBA
cf-feat-extinguish-light = Extinguish Light
cf-feat-extinguish-light-desc = Two actions, once per 10 minutes: put out a light within 120 feet, or counteract a magical one. TBA
cf-feat-fantastic-leaps = Fantastic Leaps
cf-feat-fantastic-leaps-desc = Your Leap goes 10 feet farther along and 5 feet higher. TBA
cf-feat-feathered-cloak = Feathered Cloak
cf-feat-feathered-cloak-desc = +2 circumstance to Deception to pass as a non-strix version of yourself, and +2 circumstance to Stealth to conceal an object. TBA
cf-feat-fetchling-lore = Fetchling Lore
cf-feat-fetchling-lore-desc = Trained in Occultism and Stealth.
cf-feat-fey-fellowship = Fey Fellowship
cf-feat-fey-fellowship-desc = +2 circumstance to Perception and saves against fey. The quick Make an Impression: TBA
cf-feat-fire-savvy = Fire Savvy
cf-feat-fire-savvy-desc = The flat check to end persistent fire damage is DC 10 instead of 15. A critical success on saves against smoke and ash: TBA
cf-feat-first-world-magic = First World Magic
cf-feat-first-world-magic-desc = Choose one primal cantrip. You can cast it at will.
cf-feat-fisheye = Fisheye
cf-feat-fisheye-desc = Requires the kijimuna heritage, which the game does not have. Once a day, eat a fish's eye to hold your breath for an hour. TBA
cf-feat-fledgling-flight = Fledgling Flight
cf-feat-fledgling-flight-desc = One action, once a round: Fly 15 feet, and fall if you do not land on something solid. Flying is not built yet (roadmap 2.7). TBA
cf-feat-flexible-tail = Flexible Tail
cf-feat-flexible-tail-desc = Your tail can do simple things, such as open an unlocked door. TBA
cf-feat-folksy-patter = Folksy Patter
cf-feat-folksy-patter-desc = Hide a three word message in your speech. Listeners need a DC 20 Perception check, easier for halflings. TBA
cf-feat-forlorn = Forlorn
cf-feat-forlorn-desc = +1 circumstance to saves against emotion effects, and a success becomes a critical success.
cf-feat-free-heart = Free Heart
cf-feat-free-heart-desc = The skills and skill feat of one more background, chosen for a passion. TBA
cf-feat-friendofthe-family = Friend of the Family
cf-feat-friendofthe-family-desc = Requires the heavenscribe kobold heritage, which the game does not have. +2 circumstance to Diplomacy with Tian Xia officials. TBA
cf-feat-friendofthe-sea = Friend of the Sea
cf-feat-friendofthe-sea-desc = You gain the Pet feat (TBA): a familiar from the sea, which the game does not have yet.
cf-feat-frog-geyser = Frog Geyser
cf-feat-frog-geyser-desc = Two actions: a 20 foot line of water, Fortitude save against your class or spell DC, pushing back and knocking prone on a failure. TBA
cf-feat-geckos-grip = Gecko's Grip
cf-feat-geckos-grip-desc = You gain the Combat Climber feat (TBA) and a climb Speed of 15 feet: climbing needs no check, and a success is a critical success.
cf-feat-general-training = General Training
cf-feat-general-training-desc = You gain one level 1 general feat you qualify for, chosen here.
cf-feat-glorious-gamtu = Glorious Gamtu
cf-feat-glorious-gamtu-desc = Requires the dokkaebi heritage, which the game does not have. Once a day, a hat that makes you invisible. TBA
cf-feat-gnome-obsession = Gnome Obsession
cf-feat-gnome-obsession-desc = You gain the Assurance feat for a Lore skill (TBA).
cf-feat-gnome-weapon-familiarity = Gnome Weapon Familiarity
cf-feat-gnome-weapon-familiarity-desc = For proficiency, you treat gnome weapons, the glaive and kukri one category simpler: martial as simple, advanced as martial. At level 5, a critical hit with one of them gets its critical specialization. Access to uncommon weapons: TBA
cf-feat-goblin-lore = Goblin Lore
cf-feat-goblin-lore-desc = Lore: Goblin Lore. Trained in Nature and Stealth.
cf-feat-goblin-scuttle = Goblin Scuttle
cf-feat-goblin-scuttle-desc = A reaction: when an ally ends a move next to you, you Step. TBA
cf-feat-goblin-song = Goblin Song
cf-feat-goblin-song-desc = Goblin Song, one action: Performance against an enemy's Will DC within 30 feet. On a success it takes -1 status to Perception and Will saves for 6 seconds, a minute on a critical success.
cf-feat-goblin-weapon-familiarity = Goblin Weapon Familiarity
cf-feat-goblin-weapon-familiarity-desc = For proficiency, you treat goblin weapons one category simpler: martial as simple, advanced as martial. At level 5, a critical hit with one of them gets its critical specialization. Access to uncommon weapons: TBA
cf-feat-graceful-guidance = Graceful Guidance
cf-feat-graceful-guidance-desc = Aid an ally's Reflex save, after readying with an action. TBA
cf-feat-grasping-reach = Grasping Reach
cf-feat-grasping-reach-desc = Interact to hold a two-handed weapon by its end: reach 10 feet, one die size smaller. TBA
cf-feat-grovel = Grovel
cf-feat-grovel-desc = Requires trained in Deception. Grovel, one action: Feint a creature within 30 feet. It rolls against Perception DC here, not Will DC.
cf-feat-halfling-lore = Halfling Lore
cf-feat-halfling-lore-desc = Lore: Halfling Lore. Trained in Acrobatics and Stealth.
cf-feat-halfling-luck = Halfling Luck
cf-feat-halfling-luck-desc = Free and automatic, once per long rest. Reroll a failed save or skill check, and the new result stands even if it is worse.
cf-feat-halfling-weapon-familiarity = Halfling Weapon Familiarity
cf-feat-halfling-weapon-familiarity-desc = For proficiency, you treat halfling weapons, the sling and shortsword one category simpler: martial as simple, advanced as martial. At level 5, a critical hit with one of them gets its critical specialization. Access to uncommon weapons: TBA
cf-feat-hardto-fool = Hard to Fool
cf-feat-hardto-fool-desc = +1 circumstance to Perception against illusions, and to Will saves against illusions and shadow effects.
cf-feat-harmlessly-cute = Harmlessly Cute
cf-feat-harmlessly-cute-desc = +1 circumstance bonus to initiative with Deception, and the Shameless Request feat, which is not imported. TBA
cf-feat-haughty-obstinacy = Haughty Obstinacy
cf-feat-haughty-obstinacy-desc = A success on a save against mental control is a critical success, and a failed Coerce against you is a critical failure. TBA
cf-feat-hoarders-craw = Hoarder's Craw
cf-feat-hoarders-craw-desc = Requires the dragonscaled kobold heritage. Store 100 coins or a light Bulk of precious things in your craw. TBA
cf-feat-hobgoblin-lore = Hobgoblin Lore
cf-feat-hobgoblin-lore-desc = Trained in Athletics and Crafting.
cf-feat-hobgoblin-weapon-familiarity = Hobgoblin Weapon Familiarity
cf-feat-hobgoblin-weapon-familiarity-desc = For proficiency, you treat hobgoblin weapons, composite bows, the glaive, longbow, longsword and shortbow one category simpler: martial as simple, advanced as martial. At level 5, a critical hit with one of them gets its critical specialization. Access to uncommon weapons: TBA
cf-feat-hold-mark = Hold Mark
cf-feat-hold-mark-desc = Trained in Diplomacy, Survival, Religion, and Intimidation. +1 status bonus to Saving Throw. Not applied in play yet.
cf-feat-hunters-defense = Hunter's Defense
cf-feat-hunters-defense-desc = Requires trained in Nature. A reaction, automatic, once an hour: when an animal, beast, elemental, fey, fungus or plant you can see would hit you, its attack is rolled against your Nature DC and not your AC, when that turns the hit aside.
cf-feat-hyena-familiar = Hyena Familiar
cf-feat-hyena-familiar-desc = A Tiny hyena familiar. Pick a familiar on the Pet tab. It follows you, on a stand-in body. Its familiar abilities: TBA
cf-feat-illusion-sense = Illusion Sense
cf-feat-illusion-sense-desc = +1 circumstance to Perception and Will saves against illusions. The free check when you come near one: TBA
cf-feat-iron-fists = Iron Fists
cf-feat-iron-fists-desc = Your fist Strike deals 1d6 bludgeoning.
cf-feat-iruxi-armaments = Iruxi Armaments
cf-feat-iruxi-armaments-desc = Your unarmed Strike deals 1d8 piercing.
cf-feat-jungle-strider = Jungle Strider
cf-feat-jungle-strider-desc = Forest and jungle are not difficult terrain for you, and a success on Balance on plants is a critical success. TBA
cf-feat-junk-tinker = Junk Tinker
cf-feat-junk-tinker-desc = Craft level 0 items from junk at a quarter of the price, with no shoddy penalty for you. TBA
cf-feat-juvenile-flight = Juvenile Flight
cf-feat-juvenile-flight-desc = Requires Fledgling Flight. Fledgling Flight flies 25 feet. Flying is not built yet (roadmap 2.7). TBA
cf-feat-kholo-lore = Kholo Lore
cf-feat-kholo-lore-desc = Lore: Kholo Lore. Trained in Stealth and Survival.
cf-feat-kholo-weapon-familiarity = Kholo Weapon Familiarity
cf-feat-kholo-weapon-familiarity-desc = For proficiency, you treat kholo weapons one category simpler: martial as simple, advanced as martial. At level 5, a critical hit with one of them gets its critical specialization. The flail, khopesh, mambele and war flail: TBA
cf-feat-kneecap = Kneecap
cf-feat-kneecap-desc = Kneecap, one action: a Strike at the legs. If it hits, the target loses 10 feet of Speed for 6 seconds, 15 on a critical hit. It deals its usual damage here, where the rules deal none.
cf-feat-kobold-breath = Kobold Breath
cf-feat-kobold-breath-desc = Requires the dragonscaled kobold heritage. Choose your benefactor's breath here. Kobold Breath, two actions: a 15 foot cone, 1d4 damage with a basic Reflex save against your class DC, another die at levels 3 and 5, and 1d4 rounds to recharge. The 30 foot line: TBA
cf-feat-kobold-lore = Kobold Lore
cf-feat-kobold-lore-desc = Lore: Kobold Lore. Trained in Stealth and Thievery.
cf-feat-kobold-momentum = Kobold Momentum
cf-feat-kobold-momentum-desc = Requires Kobold Breath. A critical hit recharges Kobold Breath, and a breath used the same turn rerolls 1s. TBA
cf-feat-kobold-weapon-familiarity = Kobold Weapon Familiarity
cf-feat-kobold-weapon-familiarity-desc = For proficiency, you treat kobold weapons, the greatpick, light pick and pick one category simpler: martial as simple, advanced as martial. At level 5, a critical hit with one of them gets its critical specialization. Access to uncommon weapons: TBA
cf-feat-koi-secrets = Koi Secrets
cf-feat-koi-secrets-desc = Speak with fish and use Diplomacy on them, and carp start out friendlier. TBA
cf-feat-lab-rat = Lab Rat
cf-feat-lab-rat-desc = +1 circumstance to saves against poisons and diseases, and a success becomes a critical success.
cf-feat-leech-clip = Leech-Clip
cf-feat-leech-clip-desc = Two actions: a flail Strike that hits slows the target by 10 feet for a round, 15 on a critical hit. TBA
cf-feat-left-hand-blood = Left-Hand Blood
cf-feat-left-hand-blood-desc = One action, once an hour: take 1 slashing damage to poison a held weapon, so its next hit deals 1d4 persistent poison. TBA
cf-feat-leshy-glide = Leshy Glide
cf-feat-leshy-glide-desc = Requires the leaf leshy heritage or Cat Fall. One action: glide 5 feet down and 25 feet forward. TBA
cf-feat-leshy-lore = Leshy Lore
cf-feat-leshy-lore-desc = Lore: Leshy Lore. Trained in Nature and Stealth.
cf-feat-leshy-superstition = Leshy Superstition
cf-feat-leshy-superstition-desc = Reaction, automatic. +1 circumstance to a save against a spell, when that would improve the result.
cf-feat-light-paws = Light Paws
cf-feat-light-paws-desc = Two actions: Stride and Step in either order, ignoring difficult terrain. TBA
cf-feat-lightless-litheness = Lightless Litheness
cf-feat-lightless-litheness-desc = A critical failure to Squeeze is a failure, a success to Escape is a critical success, and a critical success lets you Step away. TBA
cf-feat-lizardfolk-lore = Lizardfolk Lore
cf-feat-lizardfolk-lore-desc = Trained in Nature and Survival. Trained in a skill of your choice. That choice is not recorded yet.
cf-feat-long-nosed-form = Long-Nosed Form
cf-feat-long-nosed-form-desc = One action: take a human form until you drop it. You lose your beak while in it. TBA
cf-feat-long-tongue = Long Tongue
cf-feat-long-tongue-desc = Requires the snaptongue heritage. Touch spells and simple Interact actions by tongue reach 5 feet farther. TBA
cf-feat-loud-singer = Loud Singer
cf-feat-loud-singer-desc = Requires Goblin Song. A louder Goblin Song that reaches 60 feet. Singing at two enemies at once: TBA
cf-feat-lucky-break = Lucky Break
cf-feat-lucky-break-desc = Requires Cat's Luck. Cat's Luck also answers a failed Fortitude or Will save and a failed Acrobatics or Athletics check, still once a day.
cf-feat-magpie-snatch = Magpie Snatch
cf-feat-magpie-snatch-desc = Two actions: Stride twice and pick up an unattended object on the way. TBA
cf-feat-mariners-fire = Mariner's Fire
cf-feat-mariners-fire-desc = You can cast ignition at will. Casting it underwater: TBA
cf-feat-marsh-runner = Marsh Runner
cf-feat-marsh-runner-desc = Requires a swim Speed. Step through flooded ground and swamp, and a success on Balance on marsh is a critical success. TBA
cf-feat-martial-experience = Martial Experience
cf-feat-martial-experience-desc = Your level counts as your proficiency bonus with weapons you are untrained in. TBA
cf-feat-mountain-strategy = Mountain Strategy
cf-feat-mountain-strategy-desc = +1 circumstance bonus to damage against giants, goblins, hryngar and orcs, more with bigger weapon dice, and against anything that critically hits you for a minute. TBA
cf-feat-natural-ambition = Natural Ambition
cf-feat-natural-ambition-desc = You gain one level 1 class feat of your class, chosen here.
cf-feat-natural-skill = Natural Skill
cf-feat-natural-skill-desc = You become trained in two skills of your choice.
cf-feat-nimble-elf = Nimble Elf
cf-feat-nimble-elf-desc = Speed +5 feet.
cf-feat-noble-bloom = Noble Bloom
cf-feat-noble-bloom-desc = A reaction, automatic, once a day: an ally within 30 feet who would drop to 0 Hit Points stays at 1, and you both gain wounded 1.
cf-feat-nocturnal-tripkee = Nocturnal Tripkee
cf-feat-nocturnal-tripkee-desc = You can see in darkness.
cf-feat-one-toed-hop = One-Toed Hop
cf-feat-one-toed-hop-desc = One action: a Leap straight up that does not provoke reactions to moving. TBA
cf-feat-orc-ferocity = Orc Ferocity
cf-feat-orc-ferocity-desc = Reaction, automatic, once per long rest. When you would drop to 0 Hit Points and would not die outright, you stay at 1 Hit Point and your wounded value rises by 1.
cf-feat-orc-lore = Orc Lore
cf-feat-orc-lore-desc = Lore: Orc Lore. Trained in Athletics and Survival.
cf-feat-orc-superstition = Orc Superstition
cf-feat-orc-superstition-desc = Reaction, automatic. +1 circumstance to a save against a spell, when that would improve the result.
cf-feat-orc-weapon-familiarity = Orc Weapon Familiarity
cf-feat-orc-weapon-familiarity-desc = For proficiency, you treat orc weapons, the falchion and greataxe one category simpler: martial as simple, advanced as martial. At level 5, a critical hit with one of them gets its critical specialization. Access to uncommon weapons: TBA
cf-feat-otherworldly-magic = Otherworldly Magic
cf-feat-otherworldly-magic-desc = Choose one arcane cantrip. You can cast it at will.
cf-feat-pack-hunter = Pack Hunter
cf-feat-pack-hunter-desc = +2 circumstance bonus to Aid, and allies who Aid you get the same. TBA
cf-feat-pack-rat = Pack Rat
cf-feat-pack-rat-desc = Your mundane containers hold half again as much Bulk. TBA
cf-feat-pack-stalker = Pack Stalker
cf-feat-pack-stalker-desc = Requires expert in Stealth. You gain the Terrain Stalker feat (TBA).
cf-feat-parthenogenic-hatchling = Parthenogenic Hatchling
cf-feat-parthenogenic-hatchling-desc = +1 circumstance to saves against diseases, and a success becomes a critical success. Going longer without food and water: TBA
cf-feat-phantom-resemblance = Phantom Resemblance
cf-feat-phantom-resemblance-desc = Requires Phantom Visage and the dokkaebi heritage, which the game does not have. Once a day, Phantom Visage is a rank 3 illusory disguise for an hour. TBA
cf-feat-phantom-visage = Phantom Visage
cf-feat-phantom-visage-desc = Requires the dokkaebi heritage, which the game does not have. One action: an illusory human form that counts as a disguise. TBA
cf-feat-political-acumen = Political Acumen
cf-feat-political-acumen-desc = Requires trained in Perception. +2 circumstance to Sense Motive against elves and to your Perception DC against lies from Tanglebriar agents. TBA
cf-feat-prairie-rider = Prairie Rider
cf-feat-prairie-rider-desc = Trained in Nature. +1 circumstance bonus to Nature. Not applied in play yet.
cf-feat-pride-hunter = Pride Hunter
cf-feat-pride-hunter-desc = You can Hide behind the lesser cover your allies give. TBA
cf-feat-prodigious-climber = Prodigious Climber
cf-feat-prodigious-climber-desc = A climb Speed of 10 feet, 20 with the stickytoe heritage: climbing needs no check.
cf-feat-project-persona = Project Persona
cf-feat-project-persona-desc = One action: your armor looks like fine clothes while you wear it, until you fall unconscious. TBA
cf-feat-quick-stow-ratfolk = Quick Stow (Ratfolk)
cf-feat-quick-stow-ratfolk-desc = Requires Cheek Pouches. A free action once a round: stow a held item in your cheeks. TBA
cf-feat-rabid-sprint = Rabid Sprint
cf-feat-rabid-sprint-desc = Requires the dog kholo heritage. Rabid Sprint, two actions with both hands free: +10 feet Speed for 6 seconds, which stands in for three Strides.
cf-feat-rat-familiar = Rat Familiar
cf-feat-rat-familiar-desc = A rat familiar. Pick it on the Pet tab. It follows you, on a stand-in body. Its familiar abilities: TBA
cf-feat-rat-magic = Rat Magic
cf-feat-rat-magic-desc = Cast animal messenger once a day as a primal innate spell, and a rat always answers. TBA
cf-feat-ratfolk-lore = Ratfolk Lore
cf-feat-ratfolk-lore-desc = Lore: Ratfolk Lore. Trained in Acrobatics and Stealth.
cf-feat-ratfolk-roll = Ratfolk Roll
cf-feat-ratfolk-roll-desc = Two actions: roll down a slope at four times your Speed, taking 4d6 if you hit something. TBA
cf-feat-ratspeak = Ratspeak
cf-feat-ratspeak-desc = Speak with rodents and use Diplomacy on them. TBA
cf-feat-razzle-dazzle = Razzle-Dazzle
cf-feat-razzle-dazzle-desc = A free action once an hour: when you blind or dazzle a creature, it lasts a round longer. TBA
cf-feat-recognize-ambush = Recognize Ambush
cf-feat-recognize-ambush-desc = A free action when a fight starts: draw a weapon. TBA
cf-feat-rekindled-light = Rekindled Light
cf-feat-rekindled-light-desc = Requires Star Orb. A reaction once a day: you or an ally within 30 feet of your orb who would drop to 0 Hit Points stays at 1, with 1 wounded, and heals your level. TBA
cf-feat-remorseless-lash = Remorseless Lash
cf-feat-remorseless-lash-desc = After your melee Strike hits a frightened enemy, it cannot drop below frightened 1 until your next turn. TBA
cf-feat-reptile-speaker = Reptile Speaker
cf-feat-reptile-speaker-desc = Speak with reptiles and use Diplomacy on them. TBA
cf-feat-right-hand-blood = Right-Hand Blood
cf-feat-right-hand-blood-desc = Bleed yourself to Treat Wounds or Administer First Aid without a toolkit, with a +1 item bonus. TBA
cf-feat-ritual-reversion = Ritual Reversion
cf-feat-ritual-reversion-desc = Two actions: take the form of an ordinary plant of your kind. TBA
cf-feat-rock-runner = Rock Runner
cf-feat-rock-runner-desc = Rubble and uneven stone are not difficult terrain for you, and a success on Balance there is a critical success. TBA
cf-feat-rough-rider = Rough Rider
cf-feat-rough-rider-desc = You gain the Ride feat (TBA). The bonus to Command a goblin dog or wolf: TBA
cf-feat-runtsage = Runtsage
cf-feat-runtsage-desc = You gain the Adopted Ancestry feat (TBA). A level 1 ancestry feat from that ancestry: TBA
cf-feat-saber-teeth = Saber Teeth
cf-feat-saber-teeth-desc = Your unarmed Strike deals 1d6 piercing and is finesse.
cf-feat-scamper = Scamper
cf-feat-scamper-desc = One action beside an enemy: Stride with +5 feet of Speed and +2 circumstance to AC against reactions, ending away from enemies. TBA
cf-feat-scar-thick-skin = Scar-Thick Skin
cf-feat-scar-thick-skin-desc = The flat check to end persistent bleed damage is DC 10 instead of 15.
cf-feat-scavengers-search = Scavenger's Search
cf-feat-scavengers-search-desc = +2 circumstance bonus to Seek for objects within 30 feet. Seek only looks for creatures here. TBA
cf-feat-seedpod = Seedpod
cf-feat-seedpod-desc = Your unarmed Strike deals 1d4 bludgeoning.
cf-feat-sense-allies = Sense Allies
cf-feat-sense-allies-desc = Allies within 60 feet who would be undetected are only hidden to you, and the flat check to target them is DC 5. TBA
cf-feat-sensitive-nose = Sensitive Nose
cf-feat-sensitive-nose-desc = Imprecise scent out to 30 feet.
cf-feat-seven-changes-performance = Seven Changes Performance
cf-feat-seven-changes-performance-desc = Requires trained in Performance. You gain the Quick Disguise feat (TBA).
cf-feat-shadow-blending = Shadow Blending
cf-feat-shadow-blending-desc = A reaction: the flat check to target you while you are concealed or hidden by darkness is 2 harder. Needs darkness, which the game does not model yet. TBA
cf-feat-shadowofthe-wilds = Shadow of the Wilds
cf-feat-shadowofthe-wilds-desc = Outside towns you always count as Covering Tracks. TBA
cf-feat-shadowy-disguise = Shadowy Disguise
cf-feat-shadowy-disguise-desc = Cast illusory disguise once a day as an occult innate spell. TBA
cf-feat-shamethe-sin = Shame the Sin
cf-feat-shamethe-sin-desc = One action, once an hour, after a critical hit on a demon: it suffers its sin vulnerability, or 1d6 mental damage. TBA
cf-feat-shed-tail = Shed Tail
cf-feat-shed-tail-desc = Requires Iruxi Armaments (tail). A reaction, automatic, once a day: when you would be grabbed, you shed your tail and are not. The Stride after it, and losing your tail attack for the day: TBA
cf-feat-shrouded-magic = Shrouded Magic
cf-feat-shrouded-magic-desc = Choose one occult cantrip. You can cast it at will.
cf-feat-shrouded-mien = Shrouded Mien
cf-feat-shrouded-mien-desc = Trained in Deception, and you gain the Lengthy Diversion feat (TBA).
cf-feat-slink = Slink
cf-feat-slink-desc = Sneak 5 feet farther, and stay unobserved when you end a Sneak in dim light with cover. TBA
cf-feat-snare-genius = Snare Genius
cf-feat-snare-genius-desc = Requires expert in Crafting and Snare Crafting. Quick snares, three free ones a day, and a creature that critically fails against one is off-guard. TBA
cf-feat-snare-setter = Snare Setter
cf-feat-snare-setter-desc = Requires trained in Crafting. Trained in Crafting, and you gain the Snare Crafting feat (TBA).
cf-feat-sneaky = Sneaky
cf-feat-sneaky-desc = Sneak 5 feet farther, up to your Speed, and stay unobserved behind cover at the end of your turn. TBA
cf-feat-soaring-flight = Soaring Flight
cf-feat-soaring-flight-desc = Requires the skyborn heritage, which the game does not have. One action, once a round: Fly 20 feet. Flying is not built yet (roadmap 2.7). TBA
cf-feat-spark-fist = Spark Fist
cf-feat-spark-fist-desc = Requires expert in Crafting. One action, once a minute: until your next turn your fist deals 1 extra fire damage, and burns you the same. TBA
cf-feat-speakwith-kindred = Speak with Kindred
cf-feat-speakwith-kindred-desc = Speak with plants and fungi and use Diplomacy on them, with +2 circumstance for your own kind. TBA
cf-feat-speakwiththe-sleeping = Speak with the Sleeping
cf-feat-speakwiththe-sleeping-desc = Once a day, ask an object a question and learn its past a minute later. TBA
cf-feat-spell-survivor = Spell Survivor
cf-feat-spell-survivor-desc = Requires Orc Superstition. A critical success on a save against a caster's spell gives you resistance 1 to that caster until their next turn. TBA
cf-feat-spirit-coffin = Spirit Coffin
cf-feat-spirit-coffin-desc = Your Strikes against incorporeal creatures are magical, or gain ghost touch if already magical. TBA
cf-feat-springing-leaper = Springing Leaper
cf-feat-springing-leaper-desc = Requires expert in Athletics. Two actions to Leap twice as high, three for three times, and turning does not fail a Long Jump. TBA
cf-feat-squawk = Squawk!
cf-feat-squawk-desc = A reaction, automatic: a critical failure on Deception, Diplomacy or Intimidation is a plain failure. The witnesses being immune for a day: TBA
cf-feat-step-lively = Step Lively
cf-feat-step-lively-desc = A reaction: when a Large or bigger enemy ends a move next to you, you Step to another square beside it. TBA
cf-feat-stone-face = Stone Face
cf-feat-stone-face-desc = +1 circumstance to saves against fear. The +2 to your Will DC against Intimidation: TBA
cf-feat-stonemasons-eye = Stonemason's Eye
cf-feat-stonemasons-eye-desc = Trained in Crafting, and you gain the Specialty Crafting feat (TBA). The bonus to notice stonework: TBA
cf-feat-storms-lash = Storm's Lash
cf-feat-storms-lash-desc = You can cast electric arc at will.
cf-feat-story-crooner = Story Crooner
cf-feat-story-crooner-desc = Trained in Performance, +1 circumstance bonus to Performance checks, and you gain the Impressive Performance feat (TBA).
cf-feat-strix-defender = Strix Defender
cf-feat-strix-defender-desc = +1 circumstance bonus to Intimidation, Perception and Survival against humans, and -2 circumstance to Diplomacy with them. The bonus to damage against humans: TBA
cf-feat-strix-lore = Strix Lore
cf-feat-strix-lore-desc = Trained in Acrobatics and Nature.
cf-feat-strix-vengeance = Strix Vengeance
cf-feat-strix-vengeance-desc = A reaction, automatic, once per 10 minutes: when an enemy critically hits you or a strix ally you can see, your Strikes against it deal 1d6 more for 6 seconds. More dice with a striking weapon: TBA
cf-feat-sure-feet = Sure Feet
cf-feat-sure-feet-desc = A success on a check to Climb is a critical success. The same on Balance, and not being off-guard while doing either: TBA
cf-feat-swamp-stealth = Swamp Stealth
cf-feat-swamp-stealth-desc = Requires expert in Stealth. One action in a swamp: Take Cover, then Hide. TBA
cf-feat-swift-swimmer = Swift Swimmer
cf-feat-swift-swimmer-desc = A swim Speed of 15 feet, 25 with the wetlander heritage. Swimming is not built yet. TBA
cf-feat-tangleof-limbs = Tangle of Limbs
cf-feat-tangleof-limbs-desc = Requires dokkaebi goblin heritage or Tian Xia origin. Trained in Athletics. Also grants Titan Wrestler. TBA - action will be added
cf-feat-tenacious-net = Tenacious Net
cf-feat-tenacious-net-desc = The DC to Escape or Force Open your nets is 18, and a creature that gets out is off-guard until its next turn. TBA
cf-feat-tengu-feather-fan = Tengu Feather Fan
cf-feat-tengu-feather-fan-desc = A fan that casts gust of wind once a day, and heritage cantrips at will. TBA
cf-feat-tengu-lore = Tengu Lore
cf-feat-tengu-lore-desc = Lore: Tengu Lore. Trained in Society and Survival.
cf-feat-tengu-weapon-familiarity = Tengu Weapon Familiarity
cf-feat-tengu-weapon-familiarity-desc = For proficiency, you treat tengu weapons, the katana, khakkara, temple sword and wakizashi one category simpler: martial as simple, advanced as martial. At level 5, a critical hit with one of them gets its critical specialization. Access to uncommon weapons: TBA
cf-feat-terrifying-croak = Terrifying Croak
cf-feat-terrifying-croak-desc = Requires trained in Intimidation. Terrifying Croak, one action: Demoralize a creature within 30 feet. Keeping it from dropping below frightened 1: TBA
cf-feat-thrown-voice = Thrown Voice
cf-feat-thrown-voice-desc = Cast ventriloquism once a day as a primal innate spell, twice as a songbird strix. TBA
cf-feat-tinkering-fingers = Tinkering Fingers
cf-feat-tinkering-fingers-desc = Trained in Crafting.
cf-feat-tipthe-scales = Tip the Scales
cf-feat-tipthe-scales-desc = +1 circumstance bonus to Escape, and after you Escape a reaction to Step, Shove or Trip the creature. TBA
cf-feat-titan-slinger = Titan Slinger
cf-feat-titan-slinger-desc = A sling that hits a Large or bigger creature deals one die size more. TBA
cf-feat-touchofthe-sea = Touch of the Sea
cf-feat-touchofthe-sea-desc = You can cast gale blast at will. Choosing the spout cantrip instead: TBA
cf-feat-traditional-ways = Traditional Ways
cf-feat-traditional-ways-desc = +2 circumstance to Nature, Society and Lore about Kyonin and its elves, and +1 circumstance to saves against being made to act against your will. TBA
cf-feat-tripkee-glide = Tripkee Glide
cf-feat-tripkee-glide-desc = Requires the windweb heritage, which the game does not have. One action: glide 5 feet down and 25 feet forward. TBA
cf-feat-tripkee-lore = Tripkee Lore
cf-feat-tripkee-lore-desc = Lore: Tripkee Lore. Trained in Nature and Stealth.
cf-feat-tripkee-weapon-familiarity = Tripkee Weapon Familiarity
cf-feat-tripkee-weapon-familiarity-desc = For proficiency, you treat tripkee weapons, the blowgun, dart, hatchet, scythe and shortbow one category simpler: martial as simple, advanced as martial. At level 5, a critical hit with one of them gets its critical specialization. Access to uncommon weapons: TBA
cf-feat-tusks-orc = Tusks (Orc)
cf-feat-tusks-orc-desc = Your unarmed Strike deals 1d6 piercing.
cf-feat-unassuming-heroes = Unassuming Heroes
cf-feat-unassuming-heroes-desc = Once a day, a treat makes an animal's attack a +1 striking attack for a minute. TBA
cf-feat-unburdened-iron = Unburdened Iron
cf-feat-unburdened-iron-desc = Worn armor does not reduce your Speed. Reducing other Speed penalties by 5 feet: TBA
cf-feat-uncanny-agility = Uncanny Agility
cf-feat-uncanny-agility-desc = You gain the Steady Balance feat (TBA).
cf-feat-unconventional-weaponry = Unconventional Weaponry
cf-feat-unconventional-weaponry-desc = One uncommon simple or martial weapon of another people counts as simple for you. TBA
cf-feat-undaunted = Undaunted
cf-feat-undaunted-desc = +1 circumstance to saves against emotion effects, and a success becomes a critical success.
cf-feat-unfettered-halfling = Unfettered Halfling
cf-feat-unfettered-halfling-desc = A success to Escape or on a save against being grabbed, immobilized or restrained is a critical success, and a failed Grapple against you is a critical failure. TBA
cf-feat-unwavering-mien = Unwavering Mien
cf-feat-unwavering-mien-desc = A save against a sleep effect is one degree better. Mental effects lasting a round shorter: TBA
cf-feat-vandal = Vandal
cf-feat-vandal-desc = Trained in Thievery.
cf-feat-very-sneaky = Very Sneaky
cf-feat-very-sneaky-desc = Sneak 5 feet farther, up to your Speed, and stay unobserved behind cover at the end of your turn. TBA
cf-feat-vicious-incisors = Vicious Incisors
cf-feat-vicious-incisors-desc = Your jaws deal 1d6 piercing damage instead of 1d4. The backstabber trait: TBA
cf-feat-vigorous-health = Vigorous Health
cf-feat-vigorous-health-desc = When you would become drained, a DC 17 flat check avoids it. Drained does not exist yet. TBA
cf-feat-vomit-stomach = Vomit Stomach
cf-feat-vomit-stomach-desc = A reaction, automatic, once a day: when you would become sickened, the value is 2 lower, and you are off-guard for 6 seconds. The new save against a poison you ate: TBA
cf-feat-vulpine-scamper = Vulpine Scamper
cf-feat-vulpine-scamper-desc = Requires a fox form. In fox form you keep a Speed over 20 feet, jump with Athletics, and climb 20 feet after a running start. TBA
cf-feat-warren-navigator = Warren Navigator
cf-feat-warren-navigator-desc = Trained in Survival. Improves All results. Not applied in play yet.
cf-feat-watchful-halfling = Watchful Halfling
cf-feat-watchful-halfling-desc = +2 circumstance to Perception to Sense Motive on someone enchanted or possessed, and you can Aid their save. TBA
cf-feat-waterweave-tripkee = Waterweave Tripkee
cf-feat-waterweave-tripkee-desc = Breathe under water, and a swim Speed of 20 feet with the riverside heritage. Swimming is not built yet. TBA
cf-feat-well-groomed = Well-Groomed
cf-feat-well-groomed-desc = +2 circumstance to saves against diseases, and a success becomes a critical success.
cf-feat-well-met-traveler = Well-Met Traveler
cf-feat-well-met-traveler-desc = Trained in Diplomacy, and you gain the Hobnobber feat (TBA).
cf-feat-winglets = Winglets
cf-feat-winglets-desc = Leap 5 feet farther, Long Jump up to 10 feet past your Athletics result, and no running start needed. TBA
